      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message say what fails without this patch? As far as I can see, UFFDIO_MOVE can\u0027t currently move any slice of a swapped-out window that more than one slice mapped. `try_to_unmap_one()` marks none of its swap PTEs exclusive (`p3s_folio_mapped_by_slices()`, aosp/4390447), and `move_pages_ptes()` returns `-EBUSY` for a swap PTE that isn\u0027t exclusive.\n\nSo moving a fully written window after it was swapped out returns `-EBUSY`, or `-EAGAIN` with only the bytes before it moved. I think that\u0027s what the complete case of `uffd_move_retry_p3s` in aosp/4367975 would see without this patch. No data is lost, and userspace falls back to UFFDIO_COPY, as aosp/4312528 documents for slices that can\u0027t move.\n\nIf that\u0027s right, the patch saves that fallback rather than fixing a failure. Is there a user that needs swapped-out windows to move. If so, could the message say so? The comment above `move_compat_swap_folio()` could then say the same: none of the swap PTEs is exclusive, so the single-PTE path already refuses the first slice, not only the second.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "a19600eed357ed5fd1784a877ec41b0a2c5c72a2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
