      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the later callers need a new primitive: `mte_copy_page_tags()` only copies whole pages, and `mte_set_mem_tag_range()` (used by `mte_zero_clear_slice_tags()`) only sets one tag. The loop looks right to me for 4KB slices, and `mte_copy_page_tags()` still copies the whole page as before.\n\nLDGM and STGM work on naturally aligned blocks of `4 \u003c\u003c GMID_EL1.BS` bytes (up to 256), though. The start is rounded down to a block, and the loop copies whole blocks until it reaches or passes `x0 + x2`. Could the comment say that both addresses and the size must be multiples of 256 bytes, so that a later caller doesn\u0027t copy tags outside the range?",
