      "message": "As far as I can see, this branch can\u0027t run. `folio` is the copy that `mfill_atomic_pte_copy()` just allocated, without `__GFP_ZEROTAGS`, and it isn\u0027t mapped yet, so `page_mte_tagged(\u0026folio-\u003epage)` is false. The reused slice therefore still gets `mte_zero_clear_slice_tags()`, as before. That is also what a native process gets, because UFFDIO_COPY doesn\u0027t copy tags from the user buffer.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this hunk and the `\u003casm/mte.h\u003e` include, and add `mte_copy_tags_range()` together with its first real user instead? That looks like `p3s_mremap_copy_slice()` in aosp/4367984, then aosp/4367997. A separate arm64 patch just before aosp/4367984 would also make the `mte.S` change easy to review on its own.",
